  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual narrative as the victim of geopolitical tragedy",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the textual material ('text_chunk') which describes a personal tragedy — the loss of a child after 20 years of marriage due to Israeli bombing. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the emotional framing of the meme (collective mourning, intense grief) and the universal nature of the tragedy (loss of a child) create a strong semiotic projection where the viewer identifies with the victim described in the text. The user is projected onto the text_chunk as the person experiencing the described loss, thereby internalizing the narrative as their own or as a shared human experience.",
